WEBVTT

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:35.860
What's going on down there?

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:37.910
Nishi!

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:49.660
Oh, so he's training.

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:52.090
He sure has enthusiasm, to be training alone.

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:55.400
But it looks like it's still dark outside...

00:01:58.210 --> 00:02:00.060
Hey, Nishi! What time is it?

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.350
Nishi! What time is it?

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:06.430
Oh, you're awake, Joe.

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:07.700
Morning.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:09.820
I'm asking you what time it is!

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:12.150
The time? Uh... 4:30.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:13.630
4:30?

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:14.820
4:30 in the morning?

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:17.310
You're starting to scare me.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:21.350
Training this early... He's a freak.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:29.670
Keep it down! I'm trying to sleep!

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:31.710
Oh, sorry 'bout that.

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.170
I'll try to keep it down.

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:35.580
Goddamn piece of shit...

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:37.950
Old man...

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.970
Hey, Nishi! Where's the old man?

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:45.850
Hey, Nishi!

00:02:56.540 --> 00:03:00.870
This bike I found in the scrapyard might be useful after all!

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.270
Doesn't look like I'll be getting any more sleep anyway...

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:26.360
Huh? Waking up already?

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:28.600
Guess you're a light sleeper after all, Joe.

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:31.790
Say what you want, you thick-skinned bastard.

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:33.610
Hey, before you put that on, take a look here!

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:37.100
The old man got these for you, Joe.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:38.610
A training shirt and pants.

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:41.690
Plus a towel and a pair of athletic shoes.

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:42.570
What do you think?

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:43.990
They're all brand new.

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:51.580
Get changed quickly, then come down and wash your face!

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.590
Wow. These new things are nice.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.550
Oh, you're awake, Joe.

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:16.240
You're up early.

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:18.940
I didn't wake up, I was woken up against my will.

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:24.080
Oh, thanks for the clothes and the shoes, old man.

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:28.120
You seem to like them.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:39.400
Does Nishi always start practice this early?

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:45.090
This is a step above the training for the juvenile prison boxing tournament.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:50.310
He's trying to take off into the harsh world of pro boxing.

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:54.350
Now, time for some road work!

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:55.310
Get yourself ready, Nishi!

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:56.820
Yes!

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:01.280
All right!

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:04.780
I'll do this! I'll do it, old man!

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:10.760
One, two, one, two...

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:12.120
Keep going!

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:12.790
One, two...

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:15.700
Keep your chins up!

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:17.790
Nishi, relax your upper body!

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:19.080
R-Right...

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:40.810
Hold it, old man.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:47.410
We're not rats. Why are we running through these narrow, dirty streets?

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:51.520
Paved roads are too hard for road work.

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:53.910
It'll leave your ankles and joints aching.

00:05:54.550 --> 00:05:57.380
But you've just given me these new clothes!

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:59.420
Let's just run on the main roads for once!

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:01.840
Quit your complaining.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.920
Just shut up and run!

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:08.310
That bike's pretty noisy, but not as noisy as the guy riding it.

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:40.530
Now, then...

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:42.820
It's too early to be exhausted.

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:45.420
Let's go inside and work up another sweat!

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:47.160
Wh-What?

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:48.420
We have to do more?

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:50.370
You've gotta be kidding me!

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:52.080
My legs are all worn-out!

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:53.380
And my stomach's empty!

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:53.930
Joe!

00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:57.690
Fine, I got it.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:17.380
Well, looks like someone's dressed up quite sharply!

00:07:17.380 --> 00:07:19.210
Where are you heading off to?

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:22.710
The Japanese Boxing Association office.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.670
The Japanese Boxing Association?

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:31.740
I'm gonna get the commissioner to formally recognize the Tange Boxing Gym.

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:33.680
Who's this commissioner you're talking about?

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:36.160
Listen well, Joe.

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:39.720
If the Tange Boxing Gym is formally recognized by the Japanese Boxing Association,

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:46.690
then the day will soon be, when you and Nishi can fight in the white ring as pro boxers!

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:52.440
Your tomorrows and my dreams are about to bloom!

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:58.830
Now that's amazing, old man!

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:00.210
Now that's amazing, old man!

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:05.360
Well, I'll be off.

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:07.900
Nishi, take over coaching Joe!

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:09.880
Yeah! Got it!

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:15.150
Oh, dammit!

00:08:15.150 --> 00:08:17.760
We gotta do light jump rope for another four rounds!

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:19.860
Four rounds, eh?

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:23.190
I've already worked up a good enough sweat, and on top of that, my stomach's empty.

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:33.820
The white ring of the pros...

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:36.780
Wait for me, Rikiishi.

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:43.570
We gotta make it before it opens!

00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:44.550
<i>Nishi, where are you taking me?</i>

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:50.300
G-Good morning!

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:52.800
Hey, Nishi-kun.

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:55.660
Y-Yohko!

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:57.260
Y-Yohko!

00:08:57.740 --> 00:08:59.120
What's the matter, Joe?

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:00.550
You could at least say hello!

00:09:00.550 --> 00:09:03.310
This is Hayashi the grocer and his daughter Noriko.

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:04.790
Noriko?

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:07.310
Oh, so you're not Yohko.

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:13.020
So you're the Yabuki who fought Rikiishi, a professional six-round boxer, to a draw!

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:15.090
Let's have a look at your arm!

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:17.820
Oh, it's a little skinny, but it's pretty good!

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:20.720
Your wrists are nice and strong!

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:23.830
But your jaw looks a bit weak.

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:26.340
Now let me see your abs.

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:28.840
Not bad. You've got muscles showing!

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:31.000
Cut it out, old man!

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:32.940
I'm not some goddamn Ken doll, you know!

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:34.840
Stop it, Joe!

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:40.320
It's nothing. A boxer's gotta be at least this aggressive.

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:43.260
I'm sorry, he doesn't know his manners.

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:47.110
Joe, this man is my boss. He's employing me.

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:50.810
He may be your boss, but to me he's just a stranger!

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:53.820
No, Joe, he's your boss, too!

00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:55.870
Nishi... Boss...?

00:09:55.870 --> 00:09:56.560
Nishi... Boss...?

00:09:56.560 --> 00:09:58.320
You mean I'm gonna...?

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:01.400
That's right. You gotta do more than just boxing.

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:04.240
You gotta work! You have to work!

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:05.330
That's just common sense!

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:08.720
Working at a grocery...

00:10:09.410 --> 00:10:11.110
That's just not my style...

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:14.450
Come on, pick it up. We don't need people who are hesitant.

00:10:14.450 --> 00:10:16.840
All right, lets get to work!

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:19.340
Come on, Joe. Help me out.

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:22.300
At least introduce yourself!

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:24.350
Dammit!

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:27.200
I'm Yabuki Joe! Nice to meet ya!

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:33.560
Welcome!

00:10:34.550 --> 00:10:37.470
Hurry up! My kids are waiting at home hungry!

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:38.820
Here, thanks for the wait!

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:41.330
Welcome! Three slices of salmon, isn't it? Here you go!

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:43.830
The thicker the better.

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:45.830
I'll give you these for the low cost of 40 yen!

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:49.830
Thanks for the wait! Here you are!

00:10:51.690 --> 00:10:52.670
You want one of these?

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:53.650
Thanks for your business!

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:55.720
Thanks for your business!

00:10:57.070 --> 00:10:58.430
Thanks for waiting!

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:00.890
Just one second!

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:02.890
Hey, you there.

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:04.950
Do you work at this store?

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:06.160
Y-Yeah, but...

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:07.800
Don't give me, "Yeah, but"!

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:09.310
Hurry up and get me some shirataki!

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:11.230
I need some, too.

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:13.860
Uh, where's the shitaraki? {The misspelling is intentional}

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:15.650
Right here! This barrel!

00:11:15.650 --> 00:11:17.860
I need two packs of natto.

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:17.860
<i>Come on, hurry!</i>

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:19.990
Hey, my ginger comes first!

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:22.240
I need some preserved clams!

00:11:22.840 --> 00:11:23.870
So this is Shitaraki...

00:11:24.980 --> 00:11:26.370
Take 'em.

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:28.490
I can't take them home like that!

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:30.250
Wrap them up, will you?

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:32.340
Seriously, what's the matter with you?

00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:32.340
<i>U-Uh... right.</i>

00:11:32.340 --> 00:11:33.970
What about my natto?

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:34.980
<i>Something to wrap it in...</i>

00:11:33.970 --> 00:11:35.500
My ginger! I need my ginger!

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:38.010
What about my shirataki?

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:40.010
Hurry up!

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:42.010
How long do we have to wait?

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:43.380
Hurry it up!

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:45.810
<i>Ginger! I need my ginger!</i>

00:11:47.130 --> 00:11:49.020
Shut the fuck up!

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:51.530
Stop all that goddamn shouting!

00:11:51.530 --> 00:11:54.280
I only have two hands, you dumb buzzards!

00:11:58.470 --> 00:12:00.700
You're all so goddamn selfish!

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:04.190
I'm new here! Wait your turn, goddammit!

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:10.540
Ready, guys? Don't you dare buy from anyone but Bro Joe!

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:12.640
Roger that!

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:17.000
But you know, I just can't see Bro Joe as a grocery store clerk.

00:12:21.700 --> 00:12:24.650
Now that's weird, I don't see Bro Joe anywhere.

00:12:24.650 --> 00:12:26.290
You think he got himself fired?

00:12:26.290 --> 00:12:27.910
See, just like I thought.

00:12:27.910 --> 00:12:29.520
What do you kids want?

00:12:30.210 --> 00:12:33.120
We came to buy something from Bro Joe.

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:35.020
So, where's Joe?

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:37.530
About that...

00:12:37.530 --> 00:12:38.520
Fired?

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:40.270
No, not at all!

00:12:40.270 --> 00:12:42.530
He's doing some work inside!

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:45.530
What? Inside? You mean he's dealing with the accounts or something?

00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:48.030
Well, something like that.

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:50.460
Wow, he's doing some serious work.

00:12:50.460 --> 00:12:52.750
Hey, Sachi, do you think maybe he's...

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:53.500
What do you think?

00:12:57.310 --> 00:12:58.500
Huh?

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:02.510
What's the meaning of this? You made it too big again!

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:05.010
Cut it smaller, all right? Smaller!

00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:07.010
R-Right...

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:10.300
We're not selling mattress padding here!

00:13:11.590 --> 00:13:13.900
And what's with the way you're putting the glue on?

00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:15.520
You only need a little bit!

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:16.520
Oh, my! My!

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:19.420
Hey, Noriko!

00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:21.030
You'd better get to school, or you'll be late!

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:22.790
Right! I'll be going now!

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:24.030
Oh?

00:13:26.130 --> 00:13:27.030
Morning.

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:29.530
Oh, what are you all doing there?

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:33.390
We just wanted to see Joe at work...

00:13:33.390 --> 00:13:35.540
So how's Bro Joe's doing at his job?

00:13:36.820 --> 00:13:37.540
Pretty good.

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:43.000
Still, it's a good thing the Hayashi grocery hired a whiz kid like him.

00:13:43.570 --> 00:13:46.540
Bro's got incredibly sharp wits.

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:49.620
I think he could even be manager, if he wanted.

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:50.270
Huh?

00:13:50.270 --> 00:13:56.830
Well, if he's dealing with the accounts, that means he may come to manage the Hayashi grocery someday.

00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:57.770
Huh?

00:13:57.770 --> 00:14:00.810
And that'll mean the Hayashi grocery store will be successful!

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:02.420
That's exactly right.

00:14:02.420 --> 00:14:05.360
Don't you even know how to make a decent bag!?

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:08.240
Clean yourself off in the bath!

00:14:13.270 --> 00:14:15.250
Wow, looks like our "whiz kid" is having a bit of trouble!

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:20.100
I guessed Bro Joe was doing something like that.

00:14:20.100 --> 00:14:21.630
What was that!?

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:25.280
You're the one who said Joe would succeed the store!

00:14:25.280 --> 00:14:27.600
I'm sorry, I was wrong.

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:45.550
Well, Joe? What did you think of your first day at work?

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:53.610
Come on, you'll get used to it.

00:14:53.610 --> 00:14:56.830
The manager, his wife, and Noriko-san are all good people.

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:00.960
What is it?

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:02.330
What's so funny?

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:05.120
You've changed, Nishi.

00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:08.920
A year ago in the holding facility, you were a boss that would make crying children shut up.

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:10.300
It's really hard to imagine.

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:12.250
Come on, don't make fun of me, you dummy!

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:15.590
I'm not cut out for the grocery...

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:18.720
and I might not be able to become as great an employee as Nishi...

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:21.170
but I'll keep at it.

00:15:25.920 --> 00:15:28.360
Today was the first day I did any honest work.

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:42.680
I can't really put it into words...

00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:45.340
but this was pretty great.

00:15:47.470 --> 00:15:51.310
Now, today's the day the old man will get the commissioner to approve our gym!

00:15:51.310 --> 00:15:53.130
Let's put some food out for him.

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:55.350
Yeah.

00:16:10.370 --> 00:16:13.360
The old man's really late...

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:16.870
Don't worry. He'll come back smiling soon.

00:16:21.280 --> 00:16:22.870
That doesn't sound like the old man...

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:27.330
Is this Tange Danpei's house?

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:30.380
You guys better come to the police station immediately!

00:16:36.190 --> 00:16:39.350
This man was not only drunk, but acted violently,

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:40.920
and was arrested for fighting.

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:56.170
Th-That can't be true!

00:16:56.170 --> 00:17:00.370
S-So, Old man, what about getting the Tange Gym approved?

00:17:04.470 --> 00:17:06.260
To hell with the Tange Gym!

00:17:06.260 --> 00:17:08.940
And to hell with the recognition!

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:11.010
Pull yourself together, old man!

00:17:11.010 --> 00:17:12.860
What happened!?

00:17:12.860 --> 00:17:14.670
Shut the hell up! I've had enough of your jibber-jabber!

00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:17.470
Why don't you just get the hell out?

00:17:19.730 --> 00:17:22.440
Hey, where do you think you are?

00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:24.200
Stop right this instant!

00:17:24.200 --> 00:17:25.230
Hey, stop it!

00:17:30.180 --> 00:17:32.400
Throw him in jail until his head cools off.

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:33.470
We'll investigate tomorrow.

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:40.500
Come on! Move it!

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:42.790
Wait, dammit! I'm not drunk anymore!

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:44.760
Let me talk to them!

00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:47.660
I beg you! Let me talk to them!

00:17:47.660 --> 00:17:49.900
Please, let me talk to them!

00:17:49.900 --> 00:17:51.400
I beg you! Please!

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:01.430
Joe...

00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:02.870
Nishi...

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:04.750
I was a fool...

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:06.360
I'm sorry...

00:18:06.360 --> 00:18:09.330
I led you on in my foolishness.

00:18:10.800 --> 00:18:14.580
There's nothing I can do to make up for it...

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:17.160
Today...

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:21.160
I happily entered the Japanese Boxing Association commissioner's office.

00:18:21.650 --> 00:18:24.620
Full of hope, like the fool I was.

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:28.840
For a long time, they had brushed me off, saying they were busy.

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:32.580
So I went on in, without even stopping by the reception.

00:18:33.770 --> 00:18:36.520
There was some kind of meeting going on at the time.

00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:43.140
I noticed the faces of many boxing club chairmen I used to know.

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:47.850
<i>Such a thing.</i>

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:51.850
<i>Oh, if it isn't Tange-kun!</i>

00:18:51.850 --> 00:18:54.320
<i>So you're alive!</i>

00:18:56.060 --> 00:18:58.680
<i>Of course I'm still alive!</i>

00:18:58.680 --> 00:19:00.870
<i>Long time no see, everyone!</i>

00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:03.210
<i>Wow, this is just like the good ol' days!</i>

00:19:04.570 --> 00:19:09.820
<i>Y'know, I've found a really tough youngster, and I'm already placing my bets on him.</i>

00:19:10.870 --> 00:19:14.840
<i>He's really promising, so I want him to take the test to become a pro.</i>

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:20.530
<i>But I'll need to renew my chairman's license for that first.</i>

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:24.350
<i>I was hoping you can set me up, Otaka-kun, old buddy.</i>

00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:37.690
<i>I've seen plenty of your matches when you were a fighter,</i>

00:19:37.690 --> 00:19:43.700
<i>and I guess your risky fighting style really got to your head.</i>

00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:49.080
<i>What did you say? What are you saying?</i>

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:52.730
<i>What are you trying to say?</i>

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:55.090
<i>Have you forgotten?</i>

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:59.090
<i>You were so protective of your fighter that you beat up one of my fighters mid-match!</i>

00:19:59.090 --> 00:20:01.670
<i>You'd be drunk no matter what hour of the day,</i>

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:05.100
<i>and the ringside would always smell like alcohol!</i>

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:07.640
<i>You would shake the ropes and insult the fighters!</i>

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:10.100
<i>And you'd also engage in shouting matches with hecklers!</i>

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:14.110
<i>There was once a time when you beat up a referee who judged against one of your fighters!</i>

00:20:14.110 --> 00:20:17.820
<i>You're the cancer and the madman that the boxing world is finally rid of!</i>

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:19.780
<i>You're banned from the boxing association!</i>

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:20.540
<i>That's right!</i>

00:20:20.540 --> 00:20:23.920
<i>A musty old ghost like you, who's still stuck in the age of hooligans,</i>

00:20:23.920 --> 00:20:27.620
<i>will only cause problems if you come back!</i>

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:29.760
<i>No, I... I...</i>

00:20:29.760 --> 00:20:31.970
<i>I'm not the Tange Danpei I once was!</i>

00:20:31.970 --> 00:20:34.870
<i>You have to understand! Please, you have to understand!</i>

00:20:34.870 --> 00:20:36.880
<i>Man, he really is getting noisy.</i>

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:38.610
<i>When will he just leave?</i>

00:20:38.610 --> 00:20:40.880
<i>He sure is persistent...</i>

00:20:39.400 --> 00:20:41.780
<i>I wonder what your rookie is made of?</i>

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:43.880
<i>There are boxers who are exceedingly better.</i>

00:20:42.650 --> 00:20:44.500
<i>Now, let's continue our meeting.</i>

00:20:48.880 --> 00:20:52.280
<i>All right! I won't ask for your help anymore!</i>

00:20:52.280 --> 00:20:53.900
<i>Where's the commissioner?</i>

00:20:53.900 --> 00:20:58.070
<i>I'm gonna show my sincerity to the commissioner and get my license!</i>

00:20:58.070 --> 00:20:59.900
<i>Tange-kun...</i>

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:04.870
<i>I'm the commissioner. But no matter what you say to me...</i>

00:21:04.870 --> 00:21:09.050
<i>The commissioner can't overrule the majority vote of the chairmen.</i>

00:21:09.050 --> 00:21:11.010
<i>I'm sorry, but I can't help you.</i>

00:21:11.010 --> 00:21:13.600
<i>Commissioner, I have an amazing fighter!</i>

00:21:13.600 --> 00:21:17.180
<i>A bright, new talent that might even change the Japanese boxing league.</i>

00:21:17.180 --> 00:21:20.300
<i>He's standing by my side, waiting to take on the tomorrow!</i>

00:21:20.300 --> 00:21:23.380
<i>Please! I beg you!</i>

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:24.460
<i>Please!</i>

00:21:25.870 --> 00:21:30.390
<i>I'll repeat myself. The chairmen's opinion is the commissioner's will.</i>

00:21:30.390 --> 00:21:33.700
<i>Now everyone, let's begin our meeting regarding the world title.</i>

00:21:33.700 --> 00:21:35.150
<i>Please follow me to the meeting room.</i>

00:21:48.720 --> 00:21:50.160
<i>Wait!</i>

00:22:01.170 --> 00:22:04.050
<i>You fucking bastards!</i>

00:22:06.440 --> 00:22:10.940
By the time I came to, I had already downed some cheap liquor at a nearby bar.

00:22:10.940 --> 00:22:15.270
I then went back to the office and raised some hell.

00:22:25.400 --> 00:22:26.300
I'm sorry!

00:22:28.230 --> 00:22:29.410
I'm sorry!

00:22:29.410 --> 00:22:31.750
So you mean that our tomorrows...

00:22:31.750 --> 00:22:33.680
will never come?

00:22:53.560 --> 00:22:54.800
Rikiishi-kun...

00:22:54.800 --> 00:22:58.850
I finally understand why Rikiishi sent us that funeral wreath...

00:23:07.450 --> 00:23:10.490
S-Stop it, Joe! What's so funny?

00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:23.000
Stop laughing like that! It's creeping me out!

00:23:43.080 --> 00:23:46.020
Joe's road to becoming a pro is getting steeper.

00:23:46.020 --> 00:23:51.970
Now, for Joe, who tries to recover the tomorrow he lost when Tange Gym was denied its license,

00:23:51.970 --> 00:23:53.490
which way is tomorrow!?
